WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.468
ALEXANDRA PELOSI:<i> Mom,
 why did you choose this life?</i>

00:00:02.835 --> 00:00:04.871
NANCY PELOSI:<i> I didn't really
 choose this life.</i>

00:00:04.971 --> 00:00:06.005
It chose me.

00:00:06.105 --> 00:00:07.306
♪ (DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:00:07.406 --> 00:00:09.608
ALEXANDRA: I put the picture
of me and you there,

00:00:09.708 --> 00:00:11.744
<i> so that all my siblings
 can see I'm your favorite.</i>

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:15.548
<i> For my entire adult life,
I have been two steps behind you</i>

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:17.249
<i> with this camera,
 trying to keep up with you.</i>

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:19.084
NANCY:<i> I am a work horse,
 not a show horse.</i>

00:00:19.485 --> 00:00:22.255
<i> I was born into a family
 that was fiercely patriotic</i>

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:24.590
<i> and staunchly democratic.</i>

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:26.693
<i> Politics was the life
 that we led.</i>

00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:29.429
I have the high privilege
as the first president

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:32.432
to begin the State of the Union
message with these words:

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:33.933
Madam Speaker.

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:35.801
(CHEERING, APPLAUSE)

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:37.169
NANCY:<i> We're there to do a job.</i>

00:00:37.269 --> 00:00:40.106
(DENOUNCING CHATTER)

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:41.741
NANCY:<i> Not to keep a job.</i>

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:43.443
And we're gonna fire Pelosi!

00:00:43.543 --> 00:00:46.279
NANCY:<i> Some people count sheep
 at night, I count votes.</i>

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:49.014
I cannot take a bill
to the floor with this in it.

00:00:49.114 --> 00:00:50.583
This is, you know,
a backdoor way

00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:53.319
for something that I said
we could not cross
the threshold of.

00:00:53.653 --> 00:00:55.454
Here's what happens
in negotiations.

00:00:55.554 --> 00:00:57.790
You can't get tired.
You can never get tired.

00:00:57.890 --> 00:01:00.193
-ALEXANDRA: Are you gonna be
on your best behavior tonight?
-NANCY: Yes, I am.

00:01:00.293 --> 00:01:01.527
ALEXANDRA:
Don't do anything I wouldn't do.

00:01:01.627 --> 00:01:02.562
Thank you very much.

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:04.964
REPORTER:
Why did you tear it up?

00:01:05.064 --> 00:01:07.067
It was a total pack of lies.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:11.137
Let us pray that today,
January 6th,

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:13.840
will be an epiphany
for the American people.

00:01:15.642 --> 00:01:17.844
ALEXANDRA:
Look at the protestors
outside the Capitol.

00:01:18.311 --> 00:01:20.713
SPEAKER: Oh, my God!
How did that guy get up there?

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:23.816 line:0%
NANCY:

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:25.285 line:0%
SPEAKER 2:

00:01:25.385 --> 00:01:29.521 line:0%
NANCY:

00:01:29.955 --> 00:01:31.190
<i> Mr. Vice President,</i>

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:33.793
don't let anybody know
where you are.

00:01:34.494 --> 00:01:37.162
<i> We always knew that
 this responsibility</i>

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:39.131
<i> would take us into the night.</i>

00:01:39.398 --> 00:01:41.868
We'll stay as long as it takes.

00:01:43.202 --> 00:01:46.372
When I call the House to order,
I hope that it stays in order.

00:01:46.472 --> 00:01:49.975
If it doesn't stay in order,
I'll call it to order again.

00:01:50.076 --> 00:01:51.478
(LAUGHTER)

00:01:52.578 --> 00:01:54.747
ALEXANDRA:
<i> You're always on message.</i>

00:01:54.847 --> 00:01:56.215
There's no cracking you, huh?

00:01:56.315 --> 00:01:58.651
Well, um,
that's what you want to do,

00:01:58.751 --> 00:02:00.319
crack your mom.
(LAUGHS)

00:02:00.419 --> 00:02:01.888
ALEXANDRA: Yes, I do.
I want to crack you.

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:02.889
(LAUGHS)

